BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:FIKR: Talks Over Tea
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260916T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260916T190000
DTSTAMP:20260910T140007Z
UID:dartmouth-groups-1631521@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu
 /rsvp_boot?id=1631521\n\nDescription:\nThis Fall\, we are launching a new 
 initiative: FIKR at Dartmouth — Fellowship for Islamic Knowledge and Ref
 lection.\nFIKR is built around a simple idea: before asking students to pr
 oduce thoughtful writing\, we should first create opportunities for them t
 o read\, encounter\, question\, and think thoughtfully together. Throughou
 t the Fall\, our programming will include a Book Club\, an in-person guest
  lecture\, and a weekly series called FIKR: Talks Over Tea. The questions 
 and conversations that emerge from these experiences will then help shape 
 the Journal’s inaugural Winter publication.\nFor Week 1 of FIKR: Talks O
 ver Tea\, our opening conversation is: What Is Knowledge For? Faith\, Lear
 ning\, and Unlearning at College\nWe hope to explore questions such as: Wh
 y are we actually in college? Is knowledge primarily for career and achiev
 ement\, or should it transform who we become? What makes seeking knowledge
  meaningful in Islam? Can someone become more educated while becoming less
  wise? How should Muslims approach ideas that genuinely challenge what the
 y already believe?\nDuring the gathering\, we plan to give students a shor
 t excerpt from al-Ghazali’s Book of Knowledge on intention and the purpo
 se of learning\, with Malcolm X’s “Learning to Read” as an optional 
 accompanying text.\nProfessor Ayubi will join us as our first guest speake
 r.\nROOM TBD but hopefully Sanborn 104 (Wren Room)!\nFood Provided (Homema
 de persian saffron tea with cinnamon and Pakistiani Chai)\n\nSponsor / org
 anizer: The Dartmouth Undergraduate Muslim Journal\n\nSource: Dartmouth Gr
 oups\n\nWhy this was included: Free Food category\; explicit food-service 
 wording\; food or meal keyword in title\n\nFood availability is inferred f
 rom the source listing\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260910T140007Z
LOCATION:Private Location (register to display)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu/rsvp_boot?id=1631521
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
