CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu
 /rsvp_boot?id=1631676\nhttps://students.dartmouth.edu/fellowships/undergra
 duate-opportunities/funding-campus-experience/david-l-boren-scholarships\n
 https://students.dartmouth.edu/fellowships/postgraduate-opportunities/fund
 ing-researchexperience/boren-fellowship\nhttps://students.dartmouth.edu/fe
 llowships/undergraduate-opportunities/funding-campus-experience/critical-l
 anguage-scholarship\nhttps://students.dartmouth.edu/fellowships/undergradu
 ate-opportunities/undergraduate-scholarships/benjamin-gilman-scholarships\
 n\nDescription:\nJoin the Fellowships Office to learn about the Boren Awar
 ds\, Critical Language Scholarship (CLS)\, and Gilman Scholarship.\nBoren 
 Scholarships\nfinance undergraduate students to study language in areas un
 derrepresented in study abroad\, including Africa\, Asia\, Central & Easte
 rn Europe\, Eurasia\, Latin America\, and the Middle East.\nEligibility:\n
 U.S. Citizen\nCurrent Undergradiate\nApplied to study abroad in an applica
 ble location\nThe\nBoren Fellowship\nprovides funding for a continuous per
 iod of overseas study to promote long-term linguistic and cultural immersi
 on. These funds may be used for study abroad programs\, overseas programs 
 with a robust language component\, or direct enrollment in a foreign unive
 rsity or independent language school.\nEligibility:\nU.S. Citizen\nAt leas
 t 18 years old\nMust be matriculated for the duration of the award\nMeet a
 ll other eligibility requirements of your host institution or specific pro
 gram\nThe\nCritical Language Scholarship\n(CLS) Program provides cohorts o
 f U.S. students an opportunity to study the language and culture at univer
 sities and nonprofits around the globe. This opportunity is open to a wide
  range of students at every level of language learning.\nEligibility:\nU.S
 . Citizen or U.S. National\nAt least 18 years old\nEnrolled in an accredit
 ed undergraduate degree program or a one-year master's program\nMeet all l
 anguage requirements of the selected program\nThe\nGilman Scholarships\nsu
 pport undergraduates of limited financial means to study abroad.\nEligibil
 ity:\nU.S. Citizen\nUndergraduate student in good academic standing\nAccep
 ted into a study abroad program that is credit eligible\nPell Grant recipi
 ent\nFood provided.\nAny questions? Reach out to fellowships.office@dartmo
 uth.edu.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Scholars programs\, Undergraduate Researc
 h\, and Fellowships at Dartmouth\n\nSource: Dartmouth Groups\n\nWhy this w
 as included: explicit food-service wording\; food keyword near service con
 text in summary\n\nFood availability is inferred from the source listing\;
  verify details before attending.
