DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82544\nhttps://cglink.me/2ob/r1631598\nhttps://cglink.me/2ob/r163
 1600\nhttps://cglink.me/2ob/r1631601\nhttps://cglink.me/2ob/r1631602\nhttp
 s://cglink.me/2ob/r1631603\nhttps://cglink.me/2ob/r1631604\nhttps://cglink
 .me/2ob/r1631605\nhttps://cglink.me/2ob/r1631606\n\nDescription:\nThe SWC 
 is excited to bring you a mid-week restorative practice* with to-go health
 y snacks and journals!\nThis experiential learning opportunity will take p
 lace every Wednesday from 3:30 to 4:15pm. Each session will look something
  like this:\n- Setup mats and settle into our spaces (5- minutes)\n- Guide
 d yoga nidra (25- minutes)\n- Prompted free-write in provided journals (6 
 minutes)\n- Debrief and optional sharing time (6 min)\n- Ending session an
 d putting away mats\, journals (3 minutes)\n*mats will be provided\nWhat i
 s Yoga Nidra?\nYoga nidra is a type of meditation practice originating fro
 m ancient India\, commonly known as "yogic sleep" or "dynamic sleep." It i
 s a contemplative practice that involves following guided prompts while ly
 ing in a comfortable position through various stages of relaxation\, breat
 hing exercises\, and visualization.\nThis practice aims to induce a state 
 of deep relaxation and meditation\, similar to the liminal state between w
 aking and sleeping. This state can provide numerous physical\, emotional\,
  and mental benefits\, such as reducing stress and anxiety\, improving sle
 ep\, enhancing creativity\, and promoting overall well-being. In this stat
 e\, you may experience a sense of timelessness\, expansiveness\, and inter
 connectedness.\nRSVP via Dartmouth Groups:\nSept 23\nSept 30\nOct 7\nOct 1
 4\nOct 21\nOct 28\nNov 4\nNov 11\n\nSponsor / organizer: Student Wellness 
 Center\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was included: 
 Free Food category\n\nFood availability is inferred from the source listin
 g\; verify details before attending.
